          "sourceDoi": "10.1016/j.neulet.2020.134893",
          "targetDoi": "10.1136/bjsm.2004.016204",
          "snippet": "The relationship between cognitive performance and extreme environmental conditions has been described before [27,28]. Particularly, evaluating time estimation during an overwintering in Antarctica involves the interaction of a wide range of variables that can shape this phenomenon, such as extreme weather [10], isolated and confined conditions [34], exposure to radiation [57], and mental health [35].",
          "section": "discussion",
